# Copy to ~/.lexrender/env (chmod 600). Never commit the real file.
# Both launchd agents read it: com.lesmots.web (the LesMots app) and com.lesmots.lexrender.

# Shared by both services. The app signs sign-in sessions with it, and Lexicon Render checks them with it.
# Generate it once on this machine, straight into this file, and never print it:
#   python3 -c 'import secrets; print("LESMOTS_SESSION_SECRET=" + secrets.token_hex(32))' >> ~/.lexrender/env
LESMOTS_SESSION_SECRET=<generated on this machine>

# Lexicon Render
LEXRENDER_PUBLIC_URL=https://marine-api.tunnel.tungo.cn/lesmots
LEXRENDER_DB=$HOME/.lexrender/lexicon.db
# Remote render (paid plan) needs a model. Either a normal API key:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=            (or LESMOTS_API_KEY + LESMOTS_API_BASE + LESMOTS_MODEL)
# ...or Codex through the Codex Online API, only for the LesMots user_ids listed
# (each run is a shell-capable agent on this machine, so keep the list to people you trust;
# "*" means every paid account). Runs take minutes, and a slow one falls back to local render.
# LEXRENDER_CODEX_URL=https://marine-api.tunnel.tungo.cn/codex
# LEXRENDER_CODEX_USERS=<your LesMots user_id>
# LEXRENDER_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-6-luna
# LEXRENDER_CODEX_EFFORT=low
# LEXRENDER_CODEX_TIMEOUT=180

# LesMots web app, served at https://marine-api.tunnel.tungo.cn/lesmots-app/
LESMOTS_BASE_PATH=/lesmots-app
# Google sign-in. The OAuth client must list https://marine-api.tunnel.tungo.cn as an
# Authorized JavaScript origin. A client ID is not a secret.
LESMOTS_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<client id>.apps.googleusercontent.com
# Story generation (optional for sign-in): ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, or LESMOTS_API_KEY + LESMOTS_API_BASE + LESMOTS_MODEL.
